WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.182 --> 00:00:01.200
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.558
It's Evan, my one word is believe,

00:00:03.558 --> 00:00:04.865
and I believe in people more

00:00:04.865 --> 00:00:06.328
than they believe in themselves,

00:00:06.328 --> 00:00:07.548
and my sincere hope is that

00:00:07.548 --> 00:00:10.638
if you see in yourself what I see in you

00:00:10.638 --> 00:00:12.596
you'll be able to change the planet.

00:00:12.596 --> 00:00:13.628
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:13.628 --> 00:00:16.845
today's message is, enjoy the journey.

00:00:16.845 --> 00:00:18.629
Over to you, Eckhart Tolle.

00:00:18.629 --> 00:00:20.665
(rooster crowing)

00:00:20.665 --> 00:00:23.434
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:26.163
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:26.163 --> 00:00:30.389
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:30.389 --> 00:00:34.420
- Talking about past
and future and excessive

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.906
emphasis on past and future in your life.

00:00:36.906 --> 00:00:39.919
Yes, of course, you need to have ...

00:00:39.919 --> 00:00:42.938
There's nothing wrong
with having a certain

00:00:42.938 --> 00:00:45.623
intention on what you want to achieve,

00:00:45.623 --> 00:00:47.213
take steps towards it,

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:50.106
it's part of living
here in this dimension.

00:00:50.106 --> 00:00:51.653
You can't just say I'm never

00:00:51.653 --> 00:00:53.889
going to plan anything anymore,

00:00:53.889 --> 00:00:56.048
just take life as it comes.

00:00:56.048 --> 00:00:57.528
Well, some people try to do that,

00:00:57.528 --> 00:01:01.822
but they're not that happy
either after a while.

00:01:01.822 --> 00:01:04.137
So then your life will get very diffused

00:01:04.137 --> 00:01:06.397
and so to have an intention

00:01:06.397 --> 00:01:08.980
to make a plan, perfectly fine.

00:01:09.897 --> 00:01:11.109
Either short term plan,

00:01:11.109 --> 00:01:14.110
like I'm going to meet
you tomorrow at 4 o'clock.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:17.851
How would you ever meet
anybody if we didn't time?

00:01:17.851 --> 00:01:20.600
And future, at a practical level,

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.404
of course it's needed.

00:01:22.404 --> 00:01:25.926
the question is whether
future takes over your mind

00:01:25.926 --> 00:01:28.516
being able to use it
for practical purposes

00:01:28.516 --> 00:01:29.833
is, of course, great,

00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:32.833
but I call that clock time, is fine,

00:01:33.937 --> 00:01:36.443
but psychological time is when the future

00:01:36.443 --> 00:01:38.282
takes over your mind and your entire

00:01:38.282 --> 00:01:41.400
thought patterns are
geared only towards future,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.857
and you treat the present moment as

00:01:44.857 --> 00:01:47.263
either just a means to an end,

00:01:47.263 --> 00:01:49.436
because it enables you
to get to the next one.

00:01:49.436 --> 00:01:51.654
You're always reaching out, so to speak,

00:01:51.654 --> 00:01:54.162
internally to the next,
yet never quite here,

00:01:54.162 --> 00:01:56.995
always looking for some fulfillment there,

00:01:56.995 --> 00:02:00.203
so you can never embrace
the fullness of now.

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:02.828
Or you make the now into even an enemy.

00:02:02.828 --> 00:02:05.282
Some people are always unhappy,

00:02:05.282 --> 00:02:09.109
perhaps we all know some,
one or two people like that.

00:02:09.109 --> 00:02:09.942
- Three.

00:02:09.942 --> 00:02:11.613
(laughs)

00:02:11.613 --> 00:02:13.583
- Who are, wherever they are,

00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:16.587
they are complaining
it's never quite right.

00:02:16.587 --> 00:02:18.930
Wherever they are, or
whoever they are with,

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.600
after a little while, they're
very uncomfortable again,

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.410
and should be somewhere else.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:26.127
You know the bumper sticker
you see on some cars,

00:02:26.127 --> 00:02:28.268
there are various versions of it,

00:02:28.268 --> 00:02:30.487
says, "I'd rather be golfing."

00:02:30.487 --> 00:02:33.526
And then another one says,
"I'd rather be fishing."

00:02:33.526 --> 00:02:36.157
I'd rather be this, I'd rather be there.

00:02:36.157 --> 00:02:40.098
When I visited the
spiritual teacher Ram Dass,

00:02:40.098 --> 00:02:43.187
who lives in Hawaii, he
has a bumper sticker ...

00:02:43.187 --> 00:02:46.631
Oh, Ram Dass was the
person who, in the 70s,

00:02:46.631 --> 00:02:49.689
wrote the book Be Here Now.

00:02:49.689 --> 00:02:51.379
Anyway, he has a bumper sticker on his car

00:02:51.379 --> 00:02:54.012
that says, "I'd rather be here now."

00:02:54.012 --> 00:02:57.524
(audience laughs)

00:02:57.524 --> 00:03:00.109
And then you realize
that you can actually,

00:03:00.109 --> 00:03:04.417
you can still pursue
whatever an intention ...

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.761
Where you want to get to, a plan.

00:03:06.761 --> 00:03:08.936
I call that, it's a bit like a journey,

00:03:08.936 --> 00:03:10.370
your life is a journey.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.954
You know you want to
go from here to there.

00:03:12.954 --> 00:03:15.223
Whether you're going to
get there, we don't know.

00:03:15.223 --> 00:03:18.426
Maybe on the way you'll
branch out to somewhere else.

00:03:18.426 --> 00:03:20.686
But at least you have a certain direction.

00:03:20.686 --> 00:03:23.807
It's good to have a some
direction in your life.

00:03:23.807 --> 00:03:26.057
But while you are traveling

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:31.576
if your destination takes
up most of your attention

00:03:31.576 --> 00:03:33.469
and you're continuously focusing on there,

00:03:33.469 --> 00:03:35.564
you miss all the journey really.

00:03:35.564 --> 00:03:37.454
You can't enjoy the journey anymore.

00:03:37.454 --> 00:03:39.922
And most of your life is the journey.

00:03:39.922 --> 00:03:42.147
The arriving is relatively rare.

00:03:42.147 --> 00:03:44.406
The wedding, ahh ahh

00:03:44.406 --> 00:03:47.361
(audience laughs)

00:03:47.361 --> 00:03:50.736
And few more graduations, ahh ahh.

00:03:50.736 --> 00:03:53.401
But so those moments are not the ...

00:03:53.401 --> 00:03:56.478
Far and few between, so
the rest is the journey.

00:03:56.478 --> 00:03:58.160
And if you can't enjoy the journey,

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:01.537
which is means the step
you're taking at this moment

00:04:01.537 --> 00:04:03.096
is really the most important.

00:04:03.096 --> 00:04:05.760
Yes, of course, you know
you're going that way,

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.089
but this step is still to be enjoyed,

00:04:09.089 --> 00:04:11.960
because that's ultimately
your whole life consists

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.431
of the step you're taking at this moment.

00:04:14.431 --> 00:04:16.440
There is never anything else.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.375
- Most entrepreneurs fail, I believe,

00:04:18.375 --> 00:04:20.060
because they don't enjoy the journey.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:21.911
Because they set some
big goal for themselves,

00:04:21.911 --> 00:04:23.637
they want to have a million dollars,

00:04:23.637 --> 00:04:24.786
or they want to build this company,

00:04:24.786 --> 00:04:26.674
or whatever it is that
they want to go out and do.

00:04:26.674 --> 00:04:28.567
And they're so attached to the goal,

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.415
without the process, without the how,

00:04:30.415 --> 00:04:32.998
without the execution on a daily basis.

00:04:32.998 --> 00:04:35.056
I believe most entrepreneurs fail

00:04:35.056 --> 00:04:36.905
because all they do is have a goal,

00:04:36.905 --> 00:04:38.761
and they say, "I'm going
to do whatever it takes

00:04:38.761 --> 00:04:40.036
to go and hit that goal."

00:04:40.036 --> 00:04:42.294
But they don't enjoy
the whatever it takes.

00:04:42.294 --> 00:04:44.706
And if all you're doing
is jumping from one goal

00:04:44.706 --> 00:04:46.009
to another goal to another goal,

00:04:46.009 --> 00:04:47.235
and never enjoying the process

00:04:47.235 --> 00:04:48.671
or the journey along the way,

00:04:48.671 --> 00:04:49.817
you're never going to be fulfilled.

00:04:49.817 --> 00:04:50.760
You're never going to be happy,

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.320
you're never going to actually hit

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:54.659
most of those big goals
that you set for yourself.

00:04:54.659 --> 00:04:55.847
It comes up consistently

00:04:55.847 --> 00:04:57.608
over and over and over and over again,

00:04:57.608 --> 00:04:58.836
in all the people that I profile,

00:04:58.836 --> 00:04:59.901
from all walks of life,

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.244
from entrepreneurs to
singers to actors, musicians,

00:05:02.244 --> 00:05:06.554
politicians, business
people, athletes, everyone.

00:05:06.554 --> 00:05:08.521
You have to enjoy the grind.

00:05:08.521 --> 00:05:11.276
And a lot of people see the
grind as a negative thing.

00:05:11.276 --> 00:05:15.100
They see it as this just
constant hustle and work.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.648
And if you're working on the wrong thing,

00:05:17.648 --> 00:05:18.879
then it is a negative thing.

00:05:18.879 --> 00:05:21.338
If you threw me into your job,

00:05:21.338 --> 00:05:23.103
into whatever your business was,

00:05:23.103 --> 00:05:24.868
I would probably suffocate.

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:27.862
In most businesses, in
most jobs, in most roles,

00:05:27.862 --> 00:05:29.545
and I had part-time jobs

00:05:29.545 --> 00:05:32.298
and other jobs before starting this,

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:33.773
I suffocated.

00:05:33.773 --> 00:05:35.376
I hated it.

00:05:35.376 --> 00:05:37.960
I could only force myself
to do something for so long.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.174
You can only force
yourself to do something

00:05:40.174 --> 00:05:43.710
that you don't enjoy for
so long before you quit.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.353
'Cause it sucks.

00:05:45.353 --> 00:05:48.181
Where you have to enjoy the daily process

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:49.739
of the work that you're doing.

00:05:49.739 --> 00:05:51.876
Now, that becomes especially
hard for entrepreneurs

00:05:51.876 --> 00:05:52.944
because there's a lot of crap

00:05:52.944 --> 00:05:55.122
that we have to deal
with to build a business.

00:05:55.122 --> 00:05:56.973
There's a lot of crap
we have to deal with,

00:05:56.973 --> 00:06:00.920
and there's very minimal
results at the beginning,

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.115
as you're just getting started,

00:06:02.115 --> 00:06:03.016
as you're building up momentum,

00:06:03.016 --> 00:06:04.493
there's very small results

00:06:04.493 --> 00:06:06.542
that you're actually getting
back for your company.

00:06:06.542 --> 00:06:07.609
So it's hard to stay motivated,

00:06:07.609 --> 00:06:09.127
it's hard to keep going.

00:06:09.127 --> 00:06:10.932
So not every day is going to be amazing

00:06:10.932 --> 00:06:11.765
as an entrepreneur.

00:06:11.765 --> 00:06:13.522
In fact you're going to
have a lot of crappy days.

00:06:13.522 --> 00:06:15.161
You're going to have a lot of
days that just don't work out.

00:06:15.161 --> 00:06:16.391
A lot of days that you feel like quitting.

00:06:16.391 --> 00:06:18.488
A lot of days where you are
really hard on yourself,

00:06:18.488 --> 00:06:20.413
really negative towards yourself,

00:06:20.413 --> 00:06:21.730
saying that you're never going to make it.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.230
You're going to have a lot of
those days as an entrepreneur.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.203
The thing that gets you through

00:06:26.203 --> 00:06:28.418
is that you still enjoy the work.

00:06:28.418 --> 00:06:29.901
You may not enjoy everything else

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:31.331
around building a business,

00:06:31.331 --> 00:06:32.560
but you enjoy the work,

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.732
you enjoy creating
whatever you're creating.

00:06:34.732 --> 00:06:36.333
You enjoy dealing with your customers.

00:06:36.333 --> 00:06:37.972
Whatever it is that you need

00:06:37.972 --> 00:06:40.185
to take more responsibility
of, more ownership of,

00:06:40.185 --> 00:06:42.074
to do more consistently.

00:06:42.074 --> 00:06:43.552
I love making videos.

00:06:43.552 --> 00:06:45.151
I love helping entrepreneurs.

00:06:45.151 --> 00:06:47.124
Not every day is amazing,

00:06:47.124 --> 00:06:49.053
in my life on my YouTube channel.

00:06:49.053 --> 00:06:50.409
You know, we had the whole past month

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:52.378
of not having great audio on the videos,

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:55.416
and you guys gave me a
ton of flack for that.

00:06:55.416 --> 00:06:56.897
And, you know, well deserved.

00:06:56.897 --> 00:06:57.968
I have standards too.

00:06:57.968 --> 00:06:59.773
And we all want to make amazing videos

00:06:59.773 --> 00:07:01.830
for you guys on my team.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:03.513
So not every day's going to be special,

00:07:03.513 --> 00:07:05.690
not ever day's going to
be the best day ever.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:08.235
But net-net, I love making
videos for you guys.

00:07:08.235 --> 00:07:09.588
I love the work that I do.

00:07:09.588 --> 00:07:11.232
I wouldn't want to be
doing something else.

00:07:11.232 --> 00:07:14.442
I don't sit in my office, or sit at home,

00:07:14.442 --> 00:07:16.545
or sit here at TDS, and thinking,

00:07:16.545 --> 00:07:18.437
"Huh, I wish I could do this."

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:19.753
As soon as I get that idea,

00:07:19.753 --> 00:07:20.863
I wish I could do something else,

00:07:20.863 --> 00:07:21.849
I have to go out and do it.

00:07:21.849 --> 00:07:23.534
It means what I'm doing is wrong.

00:07:23.534 --> 00:07:25.257
It means I have to cut something

00:07:25.257 --> 00:07:26.653
that I'm doing right now,

00:07:26.653 --> 00:07:28.095
and start doing that other thing

00:07:28.095 --> 00:07:29.170
that I'm daydreaming about.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.605
You have to enjoy the work.

00:07:30.605 --> 00:07:32.655
You have to enjoy the process.

00:07:32.655 --> 00:07:35.195
And so, if you've picked a
business where you don't,

00:07:35.195 --> 00:07:36.711
that's when you quit.

00:07:36.711 --> 00:07:39.829
When people ask me, "Should
I quit on my business?"

00:07:39.829 --> 00:07:40.662
Depends.

00:07:40.662 --> 00:07:41.495
Do you still enjoy it?

00:07:41.495 --> 00:07:42.328
Do you love it?

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:43.161
Do you have the passion for it?

00:07:43.161 --> 00:07:44.539
That's the only thing that matters.

00:07:44.539 --> 00:07:45.934
If you don't enjoy it,

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:47.947
and you're just chasing the goal, quit.

00:07:47.947 --> 00:07:50.370
Right now, and move on to something else.

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:53.372
But if you do enjoy it,
and you want to keep going,

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:56.661
and you have this vision
of yourself in the future,

00:07:56.661 --> 00:07:58.589
having this big impact,

00:07:58.589 --> 00:08:00.151
then you have to keep going.

00:08:00.151 --> 00:08:01.911
And you're going to get
hit with a lot of bricks

00:08:01.911 --> 00:08:04.500
along the way, but you have to keep going

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.935
because you enjoy the work.

00:08:05.935 --> 00:08:07.369
So the question of the day today is

00:08:07.369 --> 00:08:09.012
I want to spread a
little bit of positivity.

00:08:09.012 --> 00:08:12.587
I'm curious, what do you enjoy the most

00:08:12.587 --> 00:08:14.643
about the process in your business?

00:08:14.643 --> 00:08:16.613
What's your most favorite task?

00:08:16.613 --> 00:08:17.926
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:08:17.926 --> 00:08:19.155
Really curious to find out.

00:08:19.155 --> 00:08:20.263
And if you leave a comment within

00:08:20.263 --> 00:08:22.557
the first few hours of
this video going live,

00:08:22.557 --> 00:08:25.264
you get a chance to win one
of two of our daily prizes.

00:08:25.264 --> 00:08:27.238
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Steph Reveron.

00:08:27.238 --> 00:08:29.128
Steph, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:08:29.128 --> 00:08:31.552
Your one Word, and taking that picture,

00:08:31.552 --> 00:08:32.699
and sharing it with me.

00:08:32.699 --> 00:08:34.174
It really, really means a lot to me,

00:08:34.174 --> 00:08:36.269
and I'm so glad that you enjoyed the book.

00:08:36.269 --> 00:08:37.546
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:08:37.546 --> 00:08:38.651
I believe in you.

00:08:38.651 --> 00:08:40.538
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:08:40.538 --> 00:08:42.303
And whatever your one word is,

00:08:42.303 --> 00:08:44.806
much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning,

00:08:44.806 --> 00:08:46.205
for another shot

00:08:46.205 --> 00:08:47.598
of entpresso.

00:08:47.598 --> 00:08:50.135
♫ I wake up every morning

00:08:50.135 --> 00:08:53.703
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:08:53.703 --> 00:08:56.700
(typewriter sounds)

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.041
- This is where trainers mess people up.

00:08:59.041 --> 00:09:03.846
I've had trainers who
totally just want to prove

00:09:03.846 --> 00:09:07.216
that you can never do what they do.

00:09:07.216 --> 00:09:09.017
- Yeah.
- And they have you paying.

00:09:09.017 --> 00:09:09.996
- Right.
- I know what you mean.

00:09:09.996 --> 00:09:11.267
- Just to say like, "Oh, this poor guy."

00:09:11.267 --> 00:09:12.127
- You're not as good as me.
- Right.

00:09:12.127 --> 00:09:13.974
- And they go to blast
you, like they want you ...

00:09:13.974 --> 00:09:16.475
Unless you're in pain and
you feel like you're sick,

00:09:16.475 --> 00:09:17.746
and you're throwing up, they're like,

00:09:17.746 --> 00:09:18.852
"Yeah, that's a workout, now.

00:09:18.852 --> 00:09:21.644
Look at you, yeah, you
hurt, you can't walk, great.

00:09:21.644 --> 00:09:22.477
- Yeah.

00:09:22.477 --> 00:09:25.040
- And the whole point
it, what I tell people

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.004
is treat the gym like a spa.

00:09:27.004 --> 00:09:28.521
The first time you ever go,

00:09:28.521 --> 00:09:29.997
just go in there and walk around.

00:09:29.997 --> 00:09:31.064
- Yeah.
- Touch the weights,

00:09:31.064 --> 00:09:32.091
get a drink of water,

00:09:32.091 --> 00:09:34.352
walk around, and then leave.

00:09:34.352 --> 00:09:35.992
- Right.
- And I mean literally,

00:09:35.992 --> 00:09:38.863
do that for like a week, two weeks,

00:09:38.863 --> 00:09:42.513
until you just get to the
habit of getting in that door.

00:09:42.513 --> 00:09:43.619
Because what's going
to happen is eventually

00:09:43.619 --> 00:09:44.813
you're going to start lifting,

00:09:44.813 --> 00:09:45.875
because you're there.
- Yeah.

00:09:45.875 --> 00:09:46.984
- And you're going to do something.

00:09:46.984 --> 00:09:48.011
And then you stop.

00:09:48.011 --> 00:09:49.407
Don't ever get to the
point where you're like,

00:09:49.407 --> 00:09:51.295
"I can't feel my arm."

00:09:51.295 --> 00:09:52.531
It doesn't work.

00:09:52.531 --> 00:09:55.398
People want ... they want
my body, and all this stuff,

00:09:55.398 --> 00:09:57.367
but I've been working out consistently

00:09:57.367 --> 00:09:59.171
since I was 14 years old.
- Right.

00:09:59.171 --> 00:10:02.086
- And I'm 44, 30 years ...
- 30 years.

00:10:02.086 --> 00:10:05.083
- ... of hard core, 2 hour workouts.

00:10:05.083 --> 00:10:06.477
30 years.
- Yeah.

00:10:06.477 --> 00:10:07.832
- So it doesn't happen overnight.

00:10:07.832 --> 00:10:08.665
- Nope.

00:10:08.665 --> 00:10:10.252
- You just have to enjoy the process.

00:10:10.252 --> 00:10:11.085
- Totally.

00:10:11.085 --> 00:10:13.294
- Learn to enjoy it, because
I'm sure there was a point

00:10:13.294 --> 00:10:17.284
where you started to
enjoy losing 113 pounds.

00:10:17.284 --> 00:10:18.538
- Yup, yup, yup.

00:10:18.538 --> 00:10:20.099
- And that's the only way
you're going to keep going.

00:10:20.099 --> 00:10:21.451
- Let's enjoy the journey.

00:10:21.451 --> 00:10:23.423
Not the destination.

00:10:23.423 --> 00:10:25.436
A lot of us delay our happiness.

00:10:25.436 --> 00:10:27.486
When I get to this level,
when I get my degree,

00:10:27.486 --> 00:10:29.132
when I get the kids, when I get married,

00:10:29.132 --> 00:10:30.116
I'm going to be happy.

00:10:30.116 --> 00:10:32.947
Enjoy the journey, enjoy the whole step,

00:10:32.947 --> 00:10:33.807
the whole process.

00:10:33.807 --> 00:10:35.168
Every day that you get up

00:10:35.168 --> 00:10:37.095
to strive for whatever
it is that you're after.

00:10:37.095 --> 00:10:38.736
You know I'm a goal oriented guy.

00:10:38.736 --> 00:10:39.569
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:10:39.569 --> 00:10:41.280
- But you don't celebrate when
you get to the finish line,

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:43.333
celebrate all along the way.

00:10:43.333 --> 00:10:45.111
Celebrate all along the way.

00:10:45.111 --> 00:10:46.038
- [Steve] Yeah man.

00:10:46.038 --> 00:10:47.968
- A lot of time I'll bring
a friend of mine to the gym.

00:10:47.968 --> 00:10:50.219
And let's say it's a girl
I'll bring out to the gym,

00:10:50.219 --> 00:10:52.598
and she already feels
really hot about herself.

00:10:52.598 --> 00:10:53.583
But as she goes to the gym,

00:10:53.583 --> 00:10:55.101
she begins to see her weak spots.

00:10:55.101 --> 00:10:57.480
She begins to actually
realize how far she has to go.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:59.863
And paradoxically, the very act

00:10:59.863 --> 00:11:01.752
of actually improving herself,

00:11:01.752 --> 00:11:04.867
makes her makes her
feel even more insecure.

00:11:04.867 --> 00:11:07.882
You'll see the same thing
when guys actually try to get

00:11:07.882 --> 00:11:08.802
a little bit of money going.

00:11:08.802 --> 00:11:09.897
Or let's say that they try to learn

00:11:09.897 --> 00:11:11.007
to be good with girls, right?

00:11:11.007 --> 00:11:12.812
Let's say you actually
thought your money was okay,

00:11:12.812 --> 00:11:15.321
and then you start improving
your cash situation,

00:11:15.321 --> 00:11:16.264
all of a sudden you realize,

00:11:16.264 --> 00:11:17.738
damn if I want to get
a good business going,

00:11:17.738 --> 00:11:19.752
or if I want to get my career
going with some good momentum,

00:11:19.752 --> 00:11:21.759
I've a lot further to go than I realized.

00:11:21.759 --> 00:11:23.363
Likewise, as far as girls go.

00:11:23.363 --> 00:11:24.876
Most guys actually walk
around thinking like

00:11:24.876 --> 00:11:27.294
they can win any fight,
they can pick up any girl.

00:11:27.294 --> 00:11:28.768
But when you actually go try to do it,

00:11:28.768 --> 00:11:30.121
and you realize how much you suck,

00:11:30.121 --> 00:11:32.089
It winds up making you
feel even more insecure.

00:11:32.089 --> 00:11:34.509
So, just remember that the fact

00:11:34.509 --> 00:11:35.983
that you are trying to improve yourself,

00:11:35.983 --> 00:11:38.035
it's a paradox between self-improvement

00:11:38.035 --> 00:11:39.190
and self-acceptance,

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:41.606
because the very act
of improving yourself,

00:11:41.606 --> 00:11:43.532
sometimes can make you
feel a little bit bad.

00:11:43.532 --> 00:11:45.013
What's the frame that I come from then?

00:11:45.013 --> 00:11:46.322
How do I do all the self-improvement stuff

00:11:46.322 --> 00:11:47.964
and not feel terrible?

00:11:47.964 --> 00:11:51.739
Well, what I do is I
come from a basic frame,

00:11:51.739 --> 00:11:54.572
and the basic frame is,
I am already awesome,

00:11:54.572 --> 00:11:56.712
and I'm just enjoying my journey

00:11:56.712 --> 00:11:59.180
of becoming even more awesome.

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:01.357
So I remember back when I
was first teaching bootcamps,

00:12:01.357 --> 00:12:02.220
One of the first ones I ever taught

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.617
was here in New York City.

00:12:03.617 --> 00:12:04.722
I didn't really have a lot of students,

00:12:04.722 --> 00:12:06.035
We didn't charge a lot of money,

00:12:06.035 --> 00:12:07.718
And I probably wasn't the best teacher,

00:12:07.718 --> 00:12:09.523
so you might not have wanted
to been at that bootcamp.

00:12:09.523 --> 00:12:12.024
But the point being was,

00:12:12.024 --> 00:12:14.957
I was teaching bootcamp in a Starbucks.

00:12:14.957 --> 00:12:18.006
You know, I'd sneak in to an HIV clinic,

00:12:18.006 --> 00:12:19.397
and say that I had HIV,

00:12:19.397 --> 00:12:20.992
or we'd break into a school building,

00:12:20.992 --> 00:12:22.183
and do it on milk crates.

00:12:22.183 --> 00:12:24.068
I'd be doing seminars
in those environments.

00:12:24.068 --> 00:12:25.254
And if you would've asked me

00:12:25.254 --> 00:12:26.564
if I thought what I was doing was cool,

00:12:26.564 --> 00:12:27.630
I'd say yeah, it's cool.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:31.520
Right now, I might teach a
4-500 person seminar at a hotel.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:32.831
You ask me if I think it's cool,

00:12:32.831 --> 00:12:34.469
I say it's cool.

00:12:34.469 --> 00:12:37.171
Someday I could be teaching
a 5,000 person audience

00:12:37.171 --> 00:12:38.364
in a big auditorium somewhere,

00:12:38.364 --> 00:12:41.236
like somewhere, you
know, convention center,

00:12:41.236 --> 00:12:42.879
and if you ask me if I think it's cool,

00:12:42.879 --> 00:12:44.150
I think that's cool.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.507
And if I was running
the whole damn planet,

00:12:45.507 --> 00:12:46.983
I'd think that's cool too.

00:12:46.983 --> 00:12:50.005
Where I am on my journey,
I'm loving it, okay.

00:12:50.005 --> 00:12:51.346
I love the journey.

00:12:51.346 --> 00:12:52.892
Because, as far as I'm concerned,

00:12:52.892 --> 00:12:55.232
the golden era is now.

00:12:55.232 --> 00:12:57.765
The golden era is the present moment.

00:12:57.765 --> 00:13:00.141
And wherever I am, right,

00:13:00.141 --> 00:13:01.986
if you're asking me now,
"Oh, did it suck when

00:13:01.986 --> 00:13:03.547
you taught the programs
back at Starbucks?"

00:13:03.547 --> 00:13:05.275
No, it was awesome.

00:13:05.275 --> 00:13:07.286
I was already awesome,
and enjoying my journey

00:13:07.286 --> 00:13:08.511
to become even more awesome, right.

00:13:08.511 --> 00:13:10.155
And someday if I'm teaching 5,000 people,

00:13:10.155 --> 00:13:11.797
you say, "Oh, teaching 500 people,

00:13:11.797 --> 00:13:13.069
was that too small of a crowd for you?"

00:13:13.069 --> 00:13:15.166
I'd say, "No, I was just
enjoying my journey,

00:13:15.166 --> 00:13:17.136
I was awesome, I was just enjoying

00:13:17.136 --> 00:13:19.342
being on the path to
becoming even more awesome.

